cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "No corrected Zenodo preprint version is currently planned. Please cite the v0.4.3 software/reproducibility archive below. The historical v0.4 preprint remains part of the record but its priority wording has been withdrawn."
title: "Intra-Agent Evidence Recycling"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Boticiu"
    given-names: "Ovidiu"
version: "0.4.3"
date-released: 2026-09-01
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22259801"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ovidiuboticiu/intra-agent-evidence-recycling"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22259801"
abstract: >-
  A pre-specified and frozen behavioral study of whether repeated memory records
  derived from one external source acquire excess behavioral weight in a local
  LLM agent, and whether explicit lineage metadata mitigates that effect. The
  v0.4.3 H1 behavioral contrast was later reproduced in a fresh
  same-direct-configuration-class collection under the frozen protocol.
  Post-publication forensic validation reproduced the original numerical H1/H2
  results but did not locate a public or independently verifiable pre-collection
  timestamp for the v0.4.3 preregistration artifact. A later prior-art
  reassessment also found that the historical priority claim was not sufficiently
  supported; that claim has been withdrawn. Mechanistic source-counting and
  cross-family generality remain unestablished.
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - agent memory
  - evidence recycling
  - provenance
  - lineage metadata
  - reproducibility
